From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 17:04:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] termio: add the external backend for embedder-owned ptys (ADR
 0006)

Some hosts already own a pty and a process lifecycle they cannot give up.
Windows Terminal is the case that motivated this: its ITerminalConnection
layer owns ConPTY, and its default-terminal handoff receives an already
running ConPTY from conhost, so there is no child left to spawn.

termio.External is the second backend variant. It spawns nothing. The
embedder pushes output in through ghostty_surface_write_pty_output and
receives the terminal's input through two runtime callbacks, write_pty
and resize_pty. Surfaces opt in with io_backend = external in the surface
config; everything else keeps the exec backend and is untouched.

Flow control: writePtyOutput parses on the calling thread and returns
when the bytes are consumed. That is the backpressure. A host that cannot
hand off its next read stops reading its pty, the pty buffer fills, and
the child blocks on write - the same end state Exec reaches by blocking
its gather stage when the batch ring is full, without a ring, a second
thread, or a copy of every byte. Parsing off the io thread is not new:
Exec's parse stage is its own thread and takes the same lock for the same
duration. The obligation this puts on the embedder is documented at both
the Zig and C entry points: blocking in the call is safe, blocking while
holding a lock the terminal needs is a deadlock.

resize passes the grid size out rather than letting the embedder compute
it. The embedder's pixel-to-cell arithmetic and ours must agree exactly
or the child is told a size the terminal is not using.

The core surface asks the apprt for an external config before building
the termio environment, since that environment exists only for a child we
are not going to have. A surface asking for external IO without a
write_pty callback fails at creation rather than coming up as a terminal
that renders but cannot be typed into.

zig build test: 3089 pass, 58 skip, 0 fail. Both new tests were verified
by mutation.

